# Line endings are decided in the repo, not per contributing machine.
#
# This matters concretely for two files here. A shell script saved with CRLF
# fails at the top of `curl ... | sh` on macOS/Linux (the `\r` lands up in
# `set -eu\r` and in every path), and Windows PowerShell 5.1 refuses to parse a
# here-string whose terminator is not preceded by CRLF. With core.autocrlf=true
# on a Windows checkout - which is how this repo is developed - neither outcome
# is reproducible without pinning them.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Never line-endings, never diff noise.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary

# Nothing here is a real source file with a "normal" diff; keep them explicit.
Cargo.lock text
*.html    text eol=lf
